# KIRA — ISR / C-UAS Unmanned Aerial System

**Preliminary design and system architecture of a long-endurance fixed-wing ISR / Counter-UAS platform**

**Institution:** Politecnico di Milano
**Role:** Team Leader, 5-member group
**Academic Year:** 2024–2025
**Project Type:** Aircraft Design / Preliminary UAS Design

---

## Project Overview

KIRA is a fixed-wing Unmanned Aerial System developed as a preliminary-design study for persistent **Intelligence, Surveillance and Reconnaissance (ISR)** missions with integrated **Counter-UAS capability**.

The project focused on the design of a complete deployable UAS architecture, combining:

* long-endurance persistent surveillance;
* detection, classification and tracking of aerial threats;
* modular radar, EO/IR and EW payload integration;
* mobile Ground Control Station operations;
* deployment from semi-prepared sites;
* single- and dual-UAV operating concepts.

The baseline configuration was designed for approximately **25 hours of endurance with a 125 kg mission payload**.

---

## My Role

I acted as **Team Leader of a five-member engineering team**, coordinating the one-year conceptual and preliminary design activity.

My main responsibilities included:

* project and technical coordination;
* operational scenario and CONOPS definition;
* aircraft configuration trade-offs and preliminary sizing;
* system and mission architecture definition;
* payload integration;
* mass, power and CG management;
* performance and endurance assessment;
* preliminary structural sizing;
* mobile GCS concept definition;
* multidisciplinary aircraft-level integration.

---

## Aircraft and Mission-System Integration

The preliminary design covered:

* aerodynamic and endurance-driven wing sizing;
* propulsion sizing;
* aircraft mass breakdown;
* radar, EO/IR and EW integration;
* avionics and communication architecture;
* electrical-power budgeting;
* centre-of-gravity management;
* flight-control and actuator requirements;
* operational performance assessment.

A dedicated fuel-management strategy was considered to maintain the **CG within the prescribed stability envelope throughout the mission**.

The C-UAS architecture focused on airborne detection, tracking and electronic-warfare capability. KIRA was therefore conceived as an **ISR platform with integrated C-UAS capability**, rather than as a dedicated kinetic interceptor.

---

## Structures and Airworthiness

Preliminary structural sizing was performed using **STANAG 4671** as the provisional design basis.

The analysis included:

* manoeuvre and gust load envelopes;
* aerodynamic load estimation;
* wing-root shear and bending loads;
* bending–torsion assessment;
* preliminary composite laminate sizing.

A dual-use compliance strategy was also considered, combining a civil certification baseline with subsequent military validation where required.

---

## Design Maturity

**Estimated maturity: TRL 2–3**

KIRA remained at the **conceptual / preliminary design stage**; no full-scale prototype or flight-test campaign was performed.

Identified maturation steps include payload interface definition, HIL testing, EMI/EMC testing, prototype manufacturing and progressive flight-envelope expansion.

